                    <p>A dermatologist usually finds the melanoma and does the first biopsy. A surgical oncologist or dermatologic surgeon performs the wide excision and any lymph node surgery. A pathologist examines the tissue and writes the report. For advanced disease, a medical oncologist manages immunotherapy or targeted therapy, and a radiation oncologist may help. Learn <a href="/melanoma/finding-a-melanoma-specialist" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">how to find a melanoma specialist</a>.</p>
