                    <p>They base it on the melanoma's stage. For thin, early-stage melanoma with no symptoms, scans rarely help and can cause false alarms, so a skin and lymph node exam is usually enough. Thicker tumors, a positive <a href="/melanoma/sentinel-lymph-node-biopsy" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">sentinel lymph node biopsy</a>, or symptoms like pain or weight loss prompt imaging such as CT, PET-CT, or MRI. <a href="/melanoma/melanoma-stage-meaning" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">Staging</a> guides the choice.</p>
