                  </summary>
                  <div class="mt-3 ml-7 space-y-3">
                    <p>"Clear margins" means the removed tissue has a border of normal skin all the way around the tumor. After surgery a pathologist checks the edges of the specimen under a microscope. If no melanoma cells touch the cut edge, margins are "clear" or "negative" and the tumor was fully removed. "Positive" margins mean cells reach the edge, so more surgery is usually advised. Margins appear on your <a href="/melanoma/pathology-report" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">pathology report</a>.</p>
