                    <p>Surgery for melanoma is important but rarely an emergency. Most people have their wide excision within a few weeks of diagnosis. Timing depends on booking the right surgeon, coordinating a <a href="/melanoma/sentinel-lymph-node-biopsy" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">sentinel lymph node biopsy</a> if one is planned, other health conditions, and sometimes arranging a <a href="/melanoma/finding-a-melanoma-specialist" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">second opinion</a>. A short, planned wait to line up the right team does not worsen outcomes.</p>
