                    <span>What are the main treatment options for early melanoma?</span>
                  </summary>
                  <div class="mt-3 ml-7 space-y-3">
                    <p>For melanoma confined to the skin, surgery is the mainstay. A wide local excision removes the site with a margin of healthy tissue, usually in the office or as day surgery, and cures most thin melanomas. A <a href="/melanoma/sentinel-lymph-node-biopsy" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">sentinel lymph node biopsy</a> may be added once the tumor is about 0.8 mm thick or thicker. Radiation or drug therapy is seldom needed this early. See our <a href="/melanoma/melanoma-treatment-options" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">treatment options guide</a>.</p>
