                    <span>What's the difference between wide local excision and Mohs surgery for melanoma in situ?</span>
                  </summary>
                  <div class="mt-3 ml-7 space-y-3">
                    <p>Both remove the lesion with a clear margin. Wide local excision takes the visible spot plus a measured rim of normal skin in one step, and the edges are checked afterward. Mohs surgery removes tissue in thin layers, mapping and checking each layer under the microscope during the same visit, which spares healthy skin on the face. For <a href="/melanoma/melanoma-stage-meaning" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">melanoma in situ</a>, either can be appropriate; your surgeon recommends which fits.</p>
