                    <p>The main trigger is <a href="/melanoma/breslow-depth-explained" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">tumor thickness</a>. A sentinel lymph node biopsy is generally offered once a melanoma is around 0.8 mm deep, or thinner but ulcerated, and discussed for thicker tumors. Features like a high mitotic rate can tip the decision. It's usually skipped for very thin melanomas, where node spread is unlikely. Your age and other health conditions also count. See our <a href="/melanoma/sentinel-lymph-node-biopsy" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">sentinel node guide</a>.</p>
