                  <div class="mt-3 ml-7 space-y-3">
                    <p>Both treat melanoma that has spread or has a high risk of coming back. Immunotherapy helps your own immune system recognize and attack melanoma cells, and can give long-lasting control. Targeted therapy uses pills that block a specific mutation, most often BRAF, to shrink tumors quickly. The aim is to lower recurrence risk after surgery or to control advanced disease. See our <a href="/melanoma/melanoma-treatment-options" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">treatment options guide</a>.</p>
