                  <div class="mt-3 ml-7 space-y-3">
                    <p>With immunotherapy, most side effects come from an over-active immune system: fatigue, rash, itching, diarrhea, or thyroid changes. Most are mild, but some need steroids, so report new symptoms early. Targeted therapy more often brings fever, joint aches, rash, and fatigue that ease when the dose is adjusted. Many people keep working through treatment while the oncology team checks bloodwork regularly. See our <a href="/melanoma/melanoma-treatment-options" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">treatment options guide</a>.</p>
