                  <div class="mt-3 ml-7 space-y-3">
                    <p>After a wide local excision, expect a line of stitches, some bruising, and mild soreness for a week or two. You'll get wound-care instructions and usually return in one to two weeks for stitch removal and the final <a href="/melanoma/pathology-report" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">pathology result</a>. Most people return to desk work within days, avoiding heavy lifting or stretching the area for a few weeks. Larger wounds may need a skin graft or flap. See <a href="/melanoma/what-to-expect-after-diagnosis" class="text-teal hover:text-teal/80 hover:underline transition-colors">what to expect after diagnosis</a>.</p>
